  "reviewer_note": "Least sure: end date (1904, 1905 or 1916 depending on the entry) and length (5,750 to 5,776 miles; EBSCO gives 4,600 miles in its body, which I did not use). The pin is Vladivostok because EBSCO says the first spade was turned there (Encyclopedia.com dates a Vladivostok ceremony to May 31, 1891). The EBSCO page names Irkutsk and Lake Baikal but its Chelyabinsk wording is garbled, so I used only the Oxford text for Chelyabinsk.",
